#2325; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 3256 sq. cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7 cm", "14 cm", "10 cm", "15 cm"], "options_hi": ["7 cm", "14 cm", "10 cm", "15 cm"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=80 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image010.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=80 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image010.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The base radius and height of a cylinder are 12 cm and 35 cm respectively. Find the curved surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup> of cylinder.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12 cm &#2324;&#2352; 35 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2420", "2640", "2810", "2220"], "options_hi": ["2420", "2640", "2810", "2220"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * &pi; * r * h</p><p>= 2 * (22/7) * 12 * 35</p><p>= 44 * 60</p><p>= 2640 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * &pi; * r * h</p><p>= 2 * (22/7) * 12 * 35</p><p>= 44 * 60</p><p>= 2640 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The height and base radius of a circular cone is 8 cm and 12 cm respectively. Find the volume (in cm<sup>3</sup>) of the cone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8 cm &#2324;&#2352; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; (cm<sup>3 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["384&pi;", "324&pi;", "442&pi;", "412&pi;"], "options_hi": ["384&#960;", "324&#960;", "442&#960;", "412&#960;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the cone = (1/3) * &pi; * 12 * 12 * 8</p><p>= 384&pi; cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the cone = (1/3) * &pi; * 12 * 12 * 8</p><p>= 384&pi; cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The volume of a cone and cylinder is equal. If the height of the cone and cylinder is in the ratio of 4:3 respectively, then find the respective ratio of their radius.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3:2", "9:4", "3:1", "9:2"], "options_hi": ["3:2", "9:4", "3:1", "9:2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the height of the cone and cylinder is '4h' and '3h' respectively.</p><p>Volume of cone = volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 *&#960;r<sup>2 </sup>*4h = &#960;R<sup>2</sup>*3h</p><p>(r/R)<sup>2</sup> = 9/4</p><p>r/R = 3:2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the height of the cone and cylinder is '4h' and '3h' respectively.</p><p>Volume of cone = volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 *&#960;r<sup>2 </sup>*4h = &#960;R<sup>2</sup>*3h</p><p>(r/R)<sup>2</sup> = 9/4</p><p>r/R = 3:2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The lateral surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of a cone whose radius is 2&radic;3 cm and height is 2&radic;7 cm is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 2&radic;3 cm &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 2&radic;7 cm &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376; :</p>", "options_en": ["88&radic;30/7", "50&radic;30/7", "66&radic;30/7", "72&radic;30/7"], "options_hi": ["88&radic;30/7", "50&radic;30/7", "66&radic;30/7", "72&radic;30/7"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=219 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=125 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=71 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=160 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=121 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=91 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=219 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=125 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=71 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=160 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=121 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=91 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24094/image008.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A cone is put inside a cylinder in such a way that the volume of cone is 1/8 of the volume of cylinder. If base area of cone and cylinder are equal and height of cylinder is 24 cm, find the height of cone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344;, &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; 1/8 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 24 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8 cm", "10 cm", "9 cm", "7 cm"], "options_hi": ["8 cm", "10 cm", "9 cm", "7 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cone = 1/8 * volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = 1/8 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * 24</p><p>Height of cone = 9 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cone = 1/8 * volume of cylinder</p><p>1/3 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = 1/8 * &#960;r<sup>2</sup> * 24</p><p>Height of cone = 9 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}